      "content": "It is utterly normal to feel shattered and to replay disasters in your mind, as the relief only comes when those waves finally break and you are no longer drowning in them. Though your memory of this single moment of failure might linger like a scar, life will steadily absorb you until you are mostly just a person with a story, not a forever broken man. If you can find just one small place to heal today, or someone to help you share the weight, it begins immediately to change this permanent stain into a manageable truth. I am here to listen, but please remember that one bad outcome does not define your entire worth or future capacity for goodness.",
